Mobily Git workflow showing changed files, staging actions, and a code diff" loading="lazy" width="920" height="2048" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 78vw, 320px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div></div><div class="workflow-meter" role="tablist" aria-label="Workflow steps"><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-label="01 PAIR ONCE" data-active="true"></button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="02 KEEP IT LIVE" data-active="false"></button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="03 MOVE BETWEEN" data-active="false"></button><button type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-label="04 CLOSE THE LOOP" data-active="false"></button></div></div><div class="workflow-chapters"><article class="workflow-chapter" data-story-chapter="pair" data-active="true"><div class="workflow-mobile-visual"><div class="product-frame "><div class="product-frame-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span>MOBILY / ANDROID</span><span>LIVE PRODUCT</span></div><img alt="Mobily&#x27;s secure one-time QR pairing screen on Android" loading="lazy" width="920" height="2048" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 78vw, 320px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fpairing.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="chapter-meta"><span>01</span><span>PAIR ONCE</span></div><h3>Bind your phone to the terminal.</h3><p>Scan the one-time QR code. Mobily creates a Device Key in Android Keystore and sends only its public key to the CLI.</p></article><article class="workflow-chapter" data-story-chapter="terminal" data-active="false"><div class="workflow-mobile-visual"><div class="product-frame "><div class="product-frame-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span>MOBILY / ANDROID</span><span>LIVE PRODUCT</span></div><img alt="A live Mobily terminal Session showing passing tests on Android" loading="lazy" width="920" height="2048" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 78vw, 320px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fterminal.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="chapter-meta"><span>02</span><span>KEEP IT LIVE</span></div><h3>Return to the same visible terminal.</h3><p>Receive the current Session Snapshot, send input, use special keys, and answer a waiting prompt from Android.</p></article><article class="workflow-chapter" data-story-chapter="stations" data-active="false"><div class="workflow-mobile-visual"><div class="product-frame "><div class="product-frame-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span>MOBILY / ANDROID</span><span>LIVE PRODUCT</span></div><img alt="Mobily showing multiple paired PCs and terminals and their status" loading="lazy" width="920" height="2048" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 78vw, 320px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fstations.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="chapter-meta"><span>03</span><span>MOVE BETWEEN</span></div><h3>Keep every paired PC close.</h3><p>Switch among terminals on your PC, cloud machine, home server, or laptop without scanning the pairing code again.</p></article><article class="workflow-chapter" data-story-chapter="git" data-active="false"><div class="workflow-mobile-visual"><div class="product-frame "><div class="product-frame-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span>MOBILY / ANDROID</span><span>LIVE PRODUCT</span></div><img alt="Mobily Git workflow showing changed files, staging actions, and a code diff" loading="lazy" width="920" height="2048" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" style="color:transparent" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 78vw, 320px" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fproduct%2Fgit.webp&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></div><div class="chapter-meta"><span>04</span><span>CLOSE THE LOOP</span></div><h3>Handle the small Git moments natively.</h3><p>Review diffs, stage or unstage files, switch local branches, and commit from a phone-sized interface.</p></article></div></div></div></section><section class="setup-section" id="get-started"><div class="container setup-grid"><div class="section-heading section-heading--inverse"><p class="section-kicker"><span>04</span> / START</p><h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-title-line section-title-line--ink">One command.</span><span class="section-title-line">One scan.</span></h2><p class="section-body">Start the CLI on your PC, then install the Android app from GitHub Releases or build it from source. The first Dev Tunnels run guides authentication and setup.</p></div><div class="setup-console"><div class="setup-console-title"><span>QUICK START</span><span>NODE.JS 20+</span></div><div class="setup-step"><span>01</span><div><strong>RUN ON YOUR PC</strong><div class="command-block"><span class="command-prompt" aria-hidden="true">$</span><code>npx mobily</code><button type="button" aria-label="Copy command: npx mobily"><span aria-live="polite">COPY</span></button></div></div></div><div class="setup-step"><span>02</span><div><strong>INSTALL ON ANDROID</strong><a class="button button--paper" href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DOWNLOAD ANDROID APK ↓</a><small>Pre-release APK builds are published through GitHub Releases. Prefer source? Run <code>pnpm --filter mobily-android android</code>.</small></div></div></div></div></section><section class="security-section" id="security"><div class="container security-grid"><div class="security-copy" data-reveal="true"><div class="section-heading"><p class="section-kicker"><span>03</span> / TRUST MODEL</p><h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-title-line section-title-line--ink">Your PC.</span><span class="section-title-line section-title-line--ink">Your phone.</span><span class="section-title-line">Your keys.</span></h2><p class="section-body">The private Device Key stays in Android Keystore. Each reconnect signs a fresh challenge; the CLI verifies it before opening the Session.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily/blob/main/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">READ THE SECURITY MODEL ↗</a></div><div class="security-model" data-reveal="true"><div class="security-route" role="img" aria-label="Security illustration: your PC sends an encrypted challenge through a TLS tunnel; the non-exportable key on your Android phone signs it and the PC verifies the response"><div class="security-route-meta" aria-hidden="true"><span>AUTHENTICATED SESSION</span><span>NO MOBILY RELAY</span></div><div class="security-route-canvas" aria-hidden="true"><div class="security-device security-device--pc"><div class="security-monitor"><span>&gt;_</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="security-monitor-stand"></div><strong>YOUR PC</strong><small>CLI + PUBLIC KEY</small></div><div class="security-tunnel"><strong>TLS CHANNEL</strong><div class="security-tunnel-track"><span></span><i>01</i><i>10</i><i>01</i></div><small>CHALLENGE → SIGN → VERIFY</small></div><div class="security-device security-device--phone"><div class="security-key-phone"><span>KEY</span><i></i></div><strong>YOUR PHONE</strong><small>ANDROID KEYSTORE</small></div></div><div class="security-route-legend" aria-hidden="true"><span><i class="status-dot status-dot--success"></i> PRIVATE KEY NEVER LEAVES</span><span>FRESH CHALLENGE / EVERY RECONNECT</span></div></div></div><div class="security-proofs" data-reveal="true"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>The private key stays on the phone.</h3><p>The CLI receives the Device Key&#x27;s public key, never the non-exportable private key created by Android Keystore.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Reconnects prove device identity.</h3><p>Your PC sends a fresh challenge and opens the Session only after Android signs it successfully.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Mobily operates no relay.</h3><p>Remote access uses Microsoft Dev Tunnels. Mobily does not operate a relay of its own.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="faq-section" id="faq"><div class="container faq-grid"><div data-reveal="true"><div class="section-heading"><p class="section-kicker"><span>05</span> / FAQ</p><h2 class="section-title"><span class="section-title-line section-title-line--ink">The details</span><span class="section-title-line">developers ask.</span></h2><p class="section-body">Mobily is intentionally small, explicit, and open. The repository carries the complete technical story.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily#readme" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">READ THE DOCUMENTATION ↗</a></div><div class="faq-list" data-reveal="true"><details><summary><span>01</span><strong>Is Mobily Android-only?</strong><i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>The mobile client currently targets Android. The CLI on your PC runs on Node.js 20+ across macOS, Linux, Windows, and WSL, subject to native PTY support.</p></details><details><summary><span>02</span><strong>Does Mobily only work with coding agents?</strong><i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>No. Mobily carries a normal terminal Session, so it works with shells, build tools, editors, coding agents, and other terminal-based workflows.</p></details><details><summary><span>03</span><strong>Does my terminal pass through a Mobily cloud?</strong><i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>No Mobily-operated cloud exists. Access currently uses Microsoft Dev Tunnels between your PC and phone.</p></details><details><summary><span>04</span><strong>What survives a disconnect?</strong><i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>A tmux-backed Session can survive phone disconnects and CLI restarts. The bare PTY fallback survives phone disconnects only while the CLI process remains alive.</p></details><details><summary><span>05</span><strong>Do I need an account?</strong><i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>First-time Dev Tunnels setup may ask you to sign in with GitHub or Microsoft. The phone never needs a Microsoft account.</p></details><details><summary><span>06</span><strong>How do Android updates work?</strong><i aria-hidden="true">+</i></summary><p>Install the pre-release APK from GitHub Releases, or build the Expo app from this repository (`pnpm --filter mobily-android android` or EAS). New APK builds are attached to GitHub Releases as they ship; tagged `v*` releases publish the `mobily` CLI to npm.</p></details></div></div></section></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer-grid"><div><a class="wordmark" href="#top"><span class="wordmark-lockup" aria-label="Mobily"><span class="wordmark-mark" aria-hidden="true">&gt;_</span><span>MOBILY</span></span></a><p>A secure Android companion for terminal-based development.</p></div><p class="footer-statement">NEVER MISS A<br/>CODING SESSION.</p><div class="footer-links"><a href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GITHUB ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily/releases/latest" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">RELEASES ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily#readme" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">DOCUMENTATION ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily/blob/main/SECURITY.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">SECURITY ↗</a></div></div><div class="container footer-bottom"><span>© 2026 MOBILY CONTRIBUTORS</span><a href="https://github.com/kirank55/mobily/blob/main/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MIT LICENSED ↗</a><span>BUILT IN THE OPEN.</span></div></footer>[39m

